# The build context is the repo root (compose sets `context: ../../`), and the
# repo lives on /mnt/c — DrvFs/9p, measured on this machine at 44 MB/s against
# 3.9 GB/s on ext4, with a 35x penalty on small files. Every excluded file is
# one that does not have to cross that boundary on every single build.
#
# Keep in mind what the Dockerfiles actually COPY, and do not exclude it:
#   compose/develop/sprite_generator/requirements*.txt
#   src/sprite_generator/
#   compose/develop/{collector,orchestrator,downloader}/

# Leading slash = root of the context only. Plain `images/` would also match
# src/sprite_generator/images, which is the runtime mount point.
/images/
/.git/
/.gitattributes

# Docs and ADRs. Large, churn constantly, and nothing in any image reads them.
/.ai/
/README.md
/README.md.bak

# Operator scripts run via `docker compose run` against a bind mount
# (see the sprite-worker `scripts` volume), not baked into the image.
/scripts/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Local state that must never end up in a layer.
/compose/develop/.env
/compose/develop/db/data/
*.log
